      "topic": "Mechanics",
      "subtopic": "Linear Motion",
      "question": "A car accelerates uniformly from rest to a velocity of 20 m/s in 5 seconds. Calculate the distance covered during this time.",
      "options": {
        "A": "50 m",
        "B": "100 m",
        "C": "25 m",
        "D": "40 m"
      },
      "answer": "A",
      "explanation": "Using s = ((u + v) / 2) * t with u = 0 m/s, v = 20 m/s, t = 5 s: s = ((0 + 20) / 2) * 5 = 10 * 5 = 50 m.",
      "explanation_short": "s = ((u + v)/2) * t = (20/2) * 5 = 50 m.",
      "explanation_pidgin": "Average speed na (0 + 20)/2 = 10 m/s. Multiply by 5 seconds, distance na 50 m."
    }
  ]
